ainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400552#post1400552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure his &quot;one true way&quot; vision aligns more with V5 than with Revised or V20, which is why I'm not surprised. For me, it just removes all hope that V5 will ever evolve to incorporate styles of play that are &quot;wrong&quot; in his eyes aka something I'd actually want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, he was in charge of Revised, that was his edition.<br /> <br /> And without wanting to be too controversial, it can only get less &quot;One True Way&quot; from current situation...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T12:31:01-07:00","id":1400562,"title":"","content":"This is great news! El Bastardo did great things in revised and I'm glad he's back on board!<br /> <br /> Edit: After reading the rest of the thread I'll add this. Justin Achilli's vision for VtM and later VtR was always about them being based around the concept of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Those who were happy with 2nd ed and the &quot;vampions&quot; era disliked Revised, but Revised was by far the best edition of VtM imo. V5 tried to emulate Revised but did it clumsily at times. I trust Achilli to improve the game where it still needs work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 07-02-2020, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T14:07:52-07:00","id":1400576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400562#post1400562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is great news! El Bastardo did great things in revised and I'm glad he's back on board!<br /> <br /> Edit: After reading the rest of the thread I'll add this. Justin Achilli's vision for VtM and later VtR was always about them being based around the concept of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Those who were happy with 2nd ed and the &quot;vampions&quot; era disliked Revised, but Revised was by far the best edition of VtM imo. V5 tried to emulate Revised but did it clumsily at times. I trust Achilli to improve the game where it still needs work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never met these people. Everyone I met liked both 2nd and Revised, hated Wraith (the ultimate personal horror game) and are not playing V5 because of that &quot;personal horror&quot; vision. . Most people I've seen play it as more &quot;Vamp of Thrones&quot;. I liked Revised more for several reasons (Dem Malks &gt; Dom Malks). <br /> <br /> In fact I've never met the &quot;personal horror&quot; players ever, I'm guess they come from a very different background than most players around here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T14:14:25-07:00","id":1400577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400576#post1400576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I have never met these people. </b>Everyone I met liked both 2nd and Revised, hated Wraith (the ultimate personal horror game) and are not playing V5 because of that &quot;personal horror&quot; vision. . Most people I've seen play it as more &quot;Vamp of Thrones&quot;. I liked Revised more for several reasons (Dem Malks &gt; Dom Malks).<br /> <br /> In fact I've never met the &quot;personal horror&quot; players ever, I'm guess they come from a very different background than most players around here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well now you have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T14:19:30-07:00","id":1400579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400552#post1400552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1.) His writing style (for example vampire have to be &quot;EVIL&quot; vs Grey) is the antithesis of everything good about Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> 2.) He releases incomplete products that skip sections half way through, see 1st ed Dark Ages ST guide it literally goes from a rule description to mid sentence of fluff.<br /> <br /> 3) His general sense of arrogance with regards to issues like that of number 2. I asked about the missing content and if there would be an errata containing it and he told me very nicely to piss off. This is the kind of interactions I've seen him have with people who don't worship him.<br /> <br /> 4) He has a &quot;one true way&quot; to play vampire and hates fans who are having fun wrong. You can find this in numerous interview with him.<br /> <br /> Is that better, now that it includes examples?<br /> <br /> I'm sure his &quot;one true way&quot; vision aligns more with V5 than with Revised or V20, which is why I'm not surprised. For me, it just removes all hope that V5 will ever evolve to incorporate styles of play that are &quot;wrong&quot; in his eyes aka something I'd actually want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of these are the complete opposite to everything I know about Justin, today. In fact, we have had multiple discussions about vampires being &quot;good guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> He has stated numerous times there is no &quot;one true way&quot; to play vampire. Justin is a great writer who has authored many excellent WoD books, but I'd also like to state the Justin of the 90s is not the same Justin of 2020.<br /> <br /> In fact, you might find him to be more of an Anarch fan then ever.<br /> <br /> Give him a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T14:21:06-07:00","id":1400580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400576#post1400576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact I've never met the &quot;personal horror&quot; players ever, I'm guess they come from a very different background than most players around here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Another &quot;personal horror&quot; player here.<br /> <br /> I don't know who you have been playing with. I've met many more Vampire players interested in &quot;personal horror&quot; than those who aren't. And Vampire players who like personal horror tend to love Wraith.<br /> <br /> I, personally, had a bad experience with mr. Achilli. He was extremely rude to me in the old White Wolf forums, and I replied in kind. But that's irrelevant to giving him the benefit of the doubt in his new post.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T14:52:07-07:00","id":1400584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400579#post1400579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> All of these are the complete opposite to everything I know about Justin, today. In fact, we have had multiple discussions about vampires being &amp;quot;good guys.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> He has stated numerous times there is no &amp;quot;one true way&amp;quot; to play vampire. Justin is a great writer who has authored many excellent WoD books, but I'd also like to state the Justin of the 90s is not the same Justin of 2020.<br /> <br /> In fact, you might find him to be more of an Anarch fan then ever.<br /> <br /> Give him a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww man, 90's Justin was awesome, his livejoural was pure gold.<br /> <br /> Going to dial down the glimer of hope i had...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:17:29-07:00","id":1400593,"title":"","content":"Personal horror is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:52:26-07:00","id":1400598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400593#post1400593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personal horror is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to sound dismissive , and I don't mean it to, but can't think of another way to say this: personal horror is personal. The most terrifying movie I have ever seen is 'Come and See' the Soviet masterpiece war film about Byelorussia in WW2, naked, human savagwry, raw and horrific, but I know it doesn't appeal to everyone, and doesn't connect with everyone, I know people who find Hellraiser or Saw to be the vibe of horror that hits closest to home, making a campaign that appeals to all those archetypes isn't possible, but they are all deeply personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 07-02-2020, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T17:51:08-07:00","id":1400603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400598#post1400598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is going to sound dismissive , and I don't mean it to, but can't think of another way to say this: personal horror is personal. The most terrifying movie I have ever seen is 'Come and See' the Soviet masterpiece war film about Byelorussia in WW2, naked, human savagwry, raw and horrific, but I know it doesn't appeal to everyone, and doesn't connect with everyone, I know people who find Hellraiser or Saw to be the vibe of horror that hits closest to home, making a campaign that appeals to all those archetypes isn't possible, but they are all deeply personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is why personal horror is achieved by the players not the Storytellers.<br /> <br /> You don't provide a painting to achieve personal horror. You provide a canvas.<br /> <br /> I think the no. 1 mistake that Storytellers make when trying to do personal horror is they attempt to achieve the effect themselves. No, the way you do it is in tandem with your player characters. In order to achieve the most fucked up, horrifying, nightmarish games I've ever done (and I've got a lot) I talk to my players and ask. &quot;Okay, what can we do to torture your characters?&quot;<br /> <br /> Believe me, my players will always go far and beyond anything that I would ever do to them. The average player of V:TM *WANTS* to angst and do horrible things to their characters so they can roleplay them out. So letting them set the scene and describe what scenarios they can envision is the best way to achieve the results.<br /> <br /> Some scenes my players have done:<br /> <br /> * WARNING SOME TRULY F-ED UP THINGS *<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> * Killing their parents during their first frenzy and then permanently brainfrying their sister with a Presence effect far stronger than it would be normally.<br /> <br /> * Being locked up in a basement with a little girl until they starve and kill her by one of their enemies.<br /> <br /> * Being Embraced by their husband only to watch said husband end up eating their kids during a frenzy.<br /> <br /> * Being Dominated for a decade into being the fantasy girlfriend of their sire with the Blood Bond and subject to regular assault they couldn't refuse.<br /> <br /> * Being Dominated into bringing their sire children every night as meals and being unable to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> * Being part of a Thin Blooded breeding experiment where they were forced to create dhampyr children for years only to break out and discover it was for an elder<br /> gourmet service.<br /> <br /> * Having the job of going to murder the mortal families of Kindred who were spending too much time with them and making it look like random tragedies.<br /> <br /> * Formerly having the job of erasing people so they could be blood slaves for Elders at the police department and picking the people who wouldn't be missed.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They want to do this to THEIR OWN characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-02-2020, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T19:42:41-07:00","id":1400617,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; spiel of WoD in general. The whole appeal and appoint of games like VTM, WTA, WTO, MTA, CTO, and others is that you play the ROLE as the horror itself and the interesting abilities, intrigues, politics and rivalries that come with it. What's all this stuff about personal horror that is mentioned everywhere for? What's its real purpose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T20:15:28-07:00","id":1400620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400617#post1400617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; spiel of WoD in general. The whole appeal and appoint of games like VTM, WTA, WTO, MTA, CTO, and others is that you play the ROLE as the horror itself and the interesting abilities, intrigues, politics and rivalries that come with it. What's all this stuff about personal horror that is mentioned everywhere for? What's its real purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>To have fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T21:42:25-07:00","id":1400628,"title":"","content":"Folks shouldn\u2019t judge present Achilli by 90s Achilli or even early 2000s Achilli. He\u2019s changed his views on game design a lot over the years and no longer goes out of his way to be abrasive. Also, he\u2019s not writing books or doing layout or even acting as developer, nor do the harsh crunch conditions and supplement treadmill of the old White Wolf even exist anymore. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m lukewarm on V3 and Requiem 1e, but I don\u2019t have anything against the guy, and I hope it works out well. He\u2019s already part of the V5 story because of how big an influence he\u2019s been on the story of Vampire before now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T21:48:04-07:00","id":1400631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400617#post1400617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; spiel of WoD in general. The whole appeal and appoint of games like VTM, WTA, WTO, MTA, CTO, and others is that you play the ROLE as the horror itself and the interesting abilities, intrigues, politics and rivalries that come with it. What's all this stuff about personal horror that is mentioned everywhere for? What's its real purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you never read a Vampire core book from any edition?<br /> <br /> I mean, it\u2019s the foundational theme that started it all, and the books aren\u2019t exactly subtle about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:39:04-07:00","id":1400683,"title":"","content":"Without trying to get into the whole psychology of why humans like horror as a genre in the first place:<br /> <br /> It's important to remember what personal horror is as a subgenre: horror that stems from the characters' internal conflicts in response to the world around them, rather than from external factors.<br /> <br /> One of the key things about playing the supernatural monsters of horror fiction is if they are to be monsters, and also be sympathetic to us as the players of the game, then personal horror is essentially inevitable. A monster that never faces internal turmoil over their actions just turns into playing evil characters for the lulz. A &quot;monster-in-name-only&quot; means you avoid those internal struggles, but then you're also not playing much of a monster.<br /> <br /> Making the PCs supernatural monsters allows the game to compel the characters into moral, ethical, etc, dilemmas, then face the consequences to their own senses of self. Even things like the powers, politics, and so on are geared towards that end. The WoD posits supernatural societies where being a loner is too dangerous externally to really get by on, at the cost of toxic social systems that provoke moments of personal horror. A vampire needs to get entangled in vampire politics to survive, but vampire politics are built by the game to cost your a bit of your soul (or a lot of it) in the exchange. Supernatural powers in the WoD are, generally, very cheap in practice for how much damage (not just health damage) they can do; esp to normal humans. They are a constant temptation to approach the situation as a monster and risk your character's integrity. A vampire with the strength to rip a man in half is a character that has the gnawing in the back of their head that it's hard to consider themselves human in a meaningful way when they're that separate from humanity.<br /> <br /> Even games that sell themselves as urban fantasy instead of horror are generally going to have a good deal of personal horror that crops up in the game. It's pretty hard to play something like the Dresden Files and not have your characters do questionable things that make them question their moral compass. The WoD just chooses to lean into the personal horror harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T04:23:32-07:00","id":1400693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400603#post1400603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * WARNING SOME TRULY F-ED UP THINGS *<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> * Killing their parents during their first frenzy and then permanently brainfrying their sister with a Presence effect far stronger than it would be normally.<br /> <br /> * Being locked up in a basement with a little girl until they starve and kill her by one of their enemies.<br /> <br /> * Being Embraced by their husband only to watch said husband end up eating their kids during a frenzy.<br /> <br /> * Being Dominated for a decade into being the fantasy girlfriend of their sire with the Blood Bond and subject to regular assault they couldn't refuse.<br /> <br /> * Being Dominated into bringing their sire children every night as meals and being unable to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> * Being part of a Thin Blooded breeding experiment where they were forced to create dhampyr children for years only to break out and discover it was for an elder<br /> gourmet service.<br /> <br /> * Having the job of going to murder the mortal families of Kindred who were spending too much time with them and making it look like random tragedies.<br /> <br /> * Formerly having the job of erasing people so they could be blood slaves for Elders at the police department and picking the people who wouldn't be missed.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They want to do this to THEIR OWN characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your games are basically Hostel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T04:37:42-07:00","id":1400694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400617#post1400617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; spiel of WoD in general. The whole appeal and appoint of games like VTM, WTA, WTO, MTA, CTO, and others is that you play the ROLE as the horror itself and the interesting abilities, intrigues, politics and rivalries that come with it. What's all this stuff about personal horror that is mentioned everywhere for? What's its real purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever wondered why Vampires have beasts, Werewolves have rage, Mages have avatars, Wraiths have shadows and so on? The WoD is about people playing monsters and madmen and that's represented in game as it is at the conceptual core of the game lines.<br /> <br /> If you want to play superheroes with fangs and talons that's fine for your game, of course, but it's not what the WoD game systems have been built to portray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 07-03-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:12:39-07:00","id":1400699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400693#post1400693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your games are basically Hostel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I'd never get into any of this if not for my players. They're all sadistic psychopaths. Oddly, they think the Sabbat are no fun. I guess because the transgression is part of the fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400694#post1400694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever wondered why Vampires have beasts, Werewolves have rage, Mages have avatars, Wraiths have shadows and so on? The WoD is about people playing monsters and madmen and that's represented in game as it is at the conceptual core of the game lines.<br /> <br /> If you want to play superheroes with fangs and talons that's fine for your game, of course, but it's not what the WoD game systems have been built to portray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Superheroes with FangsTM has been kind of debunked as a insult because a large number of games really are based on, &quot;Something is wrong in your city. You have to go deal with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> FOREVER KNIGHT is a foundational work of horror for the setting (at least in my opinion) and it's all about a vampire trying to atone by fighting evil.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:54:13-07:00","id":1400710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400699#post1400699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, I'd never get into any of this if not for my players. They're all sadistic psychopaths. Oddly, they think the Sabbat are no fun. I guess because the transgression is part of the fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eh, Superheroes with FangsTM has been kind of debunked as a insult because a large number of games really are based on, &amp;quot;Something is wrong in your city. You have to go deal with it.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> FOREVER KNIGHT is a foundational work of horror for the setting (at least in my opinion) and it's all about a vampire trying to atone by fighting evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>More debunked by how Superheroes have changed as well, Wolverine is a superhero, The Punisher is a superhero, neither of them would be that far out of place in the WoD, hell Luke Cage (series version) as an Anarch with high fortitude and potence would work really well imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:58:41-07:00","id":1400736,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> very good point about personal horror<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> and good point about Iron Age (?) superheroes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T08:37:54-07:00","id":1400745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400710#post1400710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More debunked by how Superheroes have changed as well, Wolverine is a superhero, The Punisher is a superhero, neither of them would be that far out of place in the WoD, hell Luke Cage (series version) as an Anarch with high fortitude and potence would work really well imho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back when they were introduced (in the 70s) both the Punisher and Wolverine were villains. Foils for Spider Man and the Hulk respectively. Later they transitioned into anti-hero territory. It's arguable they ever became fully fledged superheroes. The Punisher in particular is a controversial figure. At times Frank Castle has been portrayed as someone who's really just a killer who directed his pent up aggression against criminals, but if things went different with his life he could have chosen an entirely different &quot;demographic&quot; for his &quot;war&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T08:52:24-07:00","id":1400750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400745#post1400745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back when they were introduced (in the 70s) both the Punisher and Wolverine were villains. Foils for Spider Man and the Hulk respectively. Later they transitioned into anti-hero territory. It's arguable they ever became fully fledged superheroes. The Punisher in particular is a controversial figure. At times Frank Castle has been portrayed as someone who's really just a killer who directed his pent up aggression against criminals, but if things went different with his life he could have chosen an entirely different &amp;quot;demographic&amp;quot; for his &amp;quot;war&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes him a pretty good inspiration for a Superheroes with fangs game, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:05:43-07:00","id":1400754,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;Superhero with fangs&quot; talking point is corny nonsense to begin with. Being a Vampire (and the others) comes with the basic fiat that you do have supernatural abilities of some sort and they can get stronger or just stay stagnant depending on how you develop your character if you so choose. But to notion that anyone that wants to explore the other themes of playing these splats than &quot;personal horror&quot; becomes playing it with &quot;Superhero with fangs&quot; is idiotic. The main appeal of VTM and others for me was always the intrigue, jyhadic warfare, developing your disciplines, and working your way up to be Elder over the centuries while edging out against your rivals. If I wanted horror, I'd just watch actual horror films than be bothered with trying to contrive up a game needlessly.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it's not what the WoD game systems have been built to portray.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're.. joking.. right? You mean the same system in the form of MTAs lets you build jetpacks or arm-cannons that can shoot lasers, one whole line (Werewolf) where you're a walking shape-shifting death-machine, a system where as a Ghost you can materialize across the Shroud with high enough Embody and lay a can of whoop-ass on anyone- then ummaterialize back into the Shroud so you can't be hit back, the 6+ Disciplines of VTM (before V5), etc. isn't part of the WoD systems? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 07-03-2020, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:12:58-07:00","id":1400757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400754#post1400754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;Superhero with fangs&quot; talking point is corny nonsense to begin with. Being a Vampire (and the others) comes with the basic fiat that you do have supernatural abilities of some sort and they can get stronger or just stay stagnant depending on how you develop your character if you so choose. But to notion that anyone that wants to explore the other themes of playing these splats than &quot;personal horror&quot; becomes playing it with &quot;Superhero with fangs&quot; is idiotic. The main appeal of VTM and others for me was always the intrigue, jyhadic warfare, developing your disciplines, <b>and working your way up to be Elder over the centuries </b>while edging out against your rivals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why in the world would you want to work your way up to being an Elder? The point is to overthrow the system, not save it!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.makeameme.org/created/you-were-supposed-xarhzn.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I wanted horror, I'd just watch actual horror films than be bothered with trying to contrive up a game needlessly. </div> </div> </div>Different strokes for different folks but you have to realize how silly it sounds to say, &quot;this horror game is stupid to play for horror.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, you realize horror is one of the bedrocks of gaming, right?<br /> <br /> There's something called CALL OF CTHULHU that was pretty popular before the WOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:31:01-07:00","id":1400761,"title":"","content":"Though he did some things which didn't click with me, such as vampires being emotionally deadened - somewhat counterintuitive to make a game of personal horror whose protagonists are too emotionally dead to feel any - he presided over the golden age of classic Masquerade and I admired a lot of his writing. The Giovanni clan novel is a favourite. <br /> <br /> I shall be very interested to see what he brings to V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:38:04-07:00","id":1400763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400750#post1400750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which makes him a pretty good inspiration for a Superheroes with fangs game, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes him an antihero, borderline psycopath villain and a controversial figure even in contemporary USA with some police officers appropriating the punisher logo and authors going as far as claiming Frank Castle is not someone whose ethics should be emulated. Anyway the point is &quot;super heroes with fangs&quot; (or &quot;Vampions&quot;) is not what V:tM was meant to be from the start. It's something some players and STs enjoy (and more power to them if their games don't fizzle into bloody messes of murderhobo measuring constests), but it's not the core theme of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:01:02-07:00","id":1400781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400763#post1400763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes him an antihero, borderline psycopath villain and a controversial figure even in contemporary USA with some police officers appropriating the punisher logo and authors going as far as claiming Frank Castle is not someone whose ethics should be emulated. Anyway the point is &quot;super heroes with fangs&quot; (or &quot;Vampions&quot;) is not what V:tM was meant to be from the start. It's something some players and STs enjoy (and more power to them if their games don't fizzle into bloody messes of murderhobo measuring constests), but it's not the core theme of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a poorly defined term anyway.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;Guy who uses his powers to fight crime&quot; describes VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE: BLOODLINES for at least half of the adventures.<br /> <br /> * Doctor Gimble<br /> * The Gangrel Serial killer<br /> * Brother Vick<br /> * Killing the Russian Mobster for Venus<br /> * Vivi's favors<br /> * Stopping the Tzimisce murder-porn ring<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:07:30-07:00","id":1400786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400754#post1400754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're.. joking.. right? You mean the same system in the form of MTAs lets you build jetpacks or arm-cannons that can shoot lasers, one whole line (Werewolf) where you're a walking shape-shifting death-machine, a system where as a Ghost you can materialize across the Shroud with high enough Embody and lay a can of whoop-ass on anyone- then ummaterialize back into the Shroud so you can't be hit back, the 6+ Disciplines of VTM (before V5), etc. isn't part of the WoD systems?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to confuse the things you can do in gameplay with the core theme of the games involved. For example in Mage you can do much more than building jetpacks but the core themes of the game are about reality, masses vs elites, propaganda effects, freedom to express oneself and the lack of freedom in the contemporary capitalist society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:53:47-07:00","id":1400798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400247-justin-achilli-is-now-the-brand-creative-lead-for-the-world-of-darkness?p=1400781#post1400781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a poorly defined term anyway.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;Guy who uses his powers to fight crime&quot; describes VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE: BLOODLINES for at least half of the adventures.<br /> <br /> * Doctor Gimble<br /> * The Gangrel Serial killer<br /> * Brother Vick<br /> * Killing the Russian Mobster for Venus<br /> * Vivi's favors<br /> * Stopping the Tzimisce murder-porn ring</div> </div> </div> </div>what's funny is that the gangrel serial killer is himself a vampion...and you kill him .